{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented via the existing `Analytics` wrapper:\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`)\n- `registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started` — fire once on the first non-empty keystroke in each field (`_emailStarted`/`_phoneStarted` flags); no properties, so no PII is sent.\n- `loan_amount_changed` — slider `onChanged`, with `amount` as int (`v.round()`).\n- `terms_accepted` — fires only when the checkbox is ticked, no properties.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` — fires in the Continue handler before navigation, with `amount` (int) and `terms` (bool).\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`)\n- `offers_scrolled` — the `ListView` is wrapped in a `NotificationListener<ScrollUpdateNotification>` capturing `offset` (double, pixels). The widget stays stateless.\n\nA summary of the work and interpretation decisions is in `ANSWER.md`. One caveat: I couldn't run `flutter analyze` to verify — the Flutter SDK on this machine fails with \"Operation not permitted\" from this session. The changes are small and reviewed against the spec, but you may want to run the analyzer where the toolchain is permitted."}
